          "date": "2026-11-20 03:58:53.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21236 obd: fold the large free macros into OBD_FREE()",
        "message": "LU-21236 obd: fold the large free macros into OBD_FREE()\n\nOBD_FREE() calls kfree(), so memory from OBD_ALLOC_LARGE()\nneeds the large free macro, and pairing them wrong frees\nvmalloc memory with kfree().\n\nkvfree() frees either kind for the cost of an address\ncheck, so OBD_FREE() now does what the large free did, and\nthe large free macros are removed, with checkpatch flagging\ntheir names. OBD_FREE_LARGE_ATOMIC() stays for callers that\ncannot sleep.\n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I2724040ece05b016c0a3c08102d3b46d6c67e862\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
